# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out as CRLF, and
# anything a tool rewrites in place — Prettier, in practice — comes back with
# CRLF and shows as modified with an empty diff. That buries real changes in a
# `git status` full of files that haven't actually changed.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes what lands in the
# working tree, so the repo reads the same on Windows, macOS and CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# The lockfile is pnpm's to format. Marking it as generated keeps its enormous
# diffs collapsed in review, where they are noise rather than signal.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
